@Advanced Editor
This advanced editor menu contains some advanced features that you might not
need; you should read fileformat.doc and the other documents first. (If any
functions here would become important for most users then the subset of that
function that is appropriate may be added into other menus too.)

:oid;OID sets
This menu allows editing the mandatory and optional OID sets in the
GENERAL.DER lump. (Editing sequences of OIDs is not implemented yet.)

The menu displays the list of OIDs; yellow means mandatory, cyan means
optional, and grey means removed (it will not be saved). Any line that
begins with ... means a relative OID.

If you select any OID then you can change if it is mandatory or optional,
or remove it (it is not actually removed until the world file is saved, but
it will be marked for being removed).

When you add a OID, you must enter the OID in decimal format; if it starts
with ... then it will add a relative OID. (If you enter an absolute OID that
is supposed to be relative, it will automatically convert it.) You must then
select if it will be added to the mandatory set or optional set.

